+---
+title: Token Saver prototype
+description: Pending local tool-result transformation integration.
+---
+
+This source prototype is not included in OpenCodex 2.64.0. It is not release-qualified.
+OpenCodex retains provider routing, authentication, model selection and reasoning settings.
+Codex Token Saver supplies a local service that returns smaller tool-result text together
+with a recoverable-original reference. Stored history remains unchanged.
+
+The optional `tokenSaver` object contains `enabled`, `protocol: 1`,
+`endpoint: "http://127.0.0.1:8789"` and an absolute `tokenFile` path.
+Absence disables it. Only the separately prepared transform service understands this
+protocol. The native Token Saver backend uses the same port; automatic migration and
+service ownership are not implemented in this prototype.
+
+Responses adapter builds support matching plain text function results. Multipart,
+encrypted and compaction inputs bypass. Native steering/injection and runTurn adapters
+are unsupported. Voice, catalog and image routes are not transformed.
+
+The bundle keeps request compression unavailable until capability publication,
+reversible lifecycle controls and real transport qualification are completed.
+Use the offline source witness for evaluation. Do not treat its result as deployment
+approval or proof of lower provider billing.
