 # Responses Transport
 
+## Token Saver prototype
+
+`src/integrations/token-saver.ts` selects string tool-result messages with matching
+Responses function-call outputs and copies only those fields. The wrapper in
+`src/server/responses/request-transport.ts` runs before adapter serialization, including
+forward-auth adapters, after replay reconstruction. History owners retain the original.
+One closure per request shares bounded content decisions across adapter rebuilds.
+Its fixed loopback HTTP client ignores proxy environment variables and redirects.
+Invalid, unavailable, disabled, oversized, encrypted, multipart and compaction inputs
+bypass; native steering/injection and runTurn adapters are unsupported. It neither
+retries provider sends nor changes model/effort selection.
+
+The strict optional config is default-off. This prototype does not advertise a ready
+capability or provide automatic migration. Real socket/reconnect and lifecycle qualification
+remain pending. Contract coverage is in `tests/responses/token-saver.test.ts`; the isolated
+bundle harness enables `tests/responses/token-saver-wire.test.ts` and
+`tests/responses/token-saver-pipeline.test.ts`. The latter exercises prepared WebSocket
+turns at the Responses core, not a real WebSocket connection.
+
 Native result continuations and function-result injection follow [the mode-specific result and control contract](streaming-health.md#experimental-native-function-result-injection); this surface does not infer upstream support or alter its defaults.
 
 Native steering follows [the shared WebSocket contract](streaming-health.md#experimental-native-mid-turn-steering); this surface's defaults remain unchanged.
